				<guid>https://ideal-stingray.github.io/example_ficsite/tags/weesnaw-pebbit/</guid>
				<description>&lt;p&gt;If you want to use tags with &lt;code&gt;/&lt;/code&gt; in them, you’ll need to&#xA;do something like this. In the frontmatter of your work you would&#xA;write:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;tags = [&amp;quot;weesnaw-pebbit&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;au&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;complete&amp;quot;]&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Once you create the &lt;code&gt;weesnaw-pebbit/_index.md&lt;/code&gt; file and&#xA;make the title &lt;code&gt;&#34;weesnaw/pebbit&#34;&lt;/code&gt;, the tag will show up&#xA;properly as &lt;code&gt;&#34;weesnaw/pebbit&#34;&lt;/code&gt;. (Tags without the&#xA;&lt;code&gt;/&lt;/code&gt; character should Just Work without you needing to create&#xA;any files for them, although you can also do that if you want to write&#xA;text on the tag page, like this.)&lt;/p&gt;</description>
